{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990562-dealing-with-pc-s-going-too-op","id":990562,"title":"Dealing with PC's going too OP","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-20T12:41:31-07:00","id":990562,"title":"Dealing with PC's going too OP","content":"So, i got a rank 3 get of fenris. she is pretty buffed up right now. I throw her enemies but she keeps going higher and stronger (dealing massive ammounts of damage and soaking A LOT). which made me think..<br /> how do you guys deal with PC's going too high caliber? how do you make threats that they can't fight against or hold them against the ropes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T13:40:47-07:00","id":990601,"title":"","content":"An Adren combat focused Garou should should one of the most dangerous things walking. Also, if that's what your player made talk to them a bit. Do they want to have fights that are more dangerous/harder, or do they like some threat but like being the furry blender of doom?<br /> <br /> As for ways to make combat more challenging:<br /> <br /> 1) Have fights in places where the Veil matters. This is probably one of the biggest things that can tamp down on Garou in fights. Even if they know and have plans, it's a giant complication to have to deal with.<br /> <br /> 2) Numbers, numbers, numbers. It can be a pain as a ST, but swarms are inherently hard on PCs in the WoD system. Defense is hard to maintain, and random Soak means eventually damage gets through. Eventually a big enough group will wear down any Garou.<br /> <br /> 3) Multi-stage fights. Even if it's just &quot;one scene&quot; for specific powers/Gifts, having to deal with waves without time to relax/recover resources is similar to the swarm issue. It creates a tactical choice of having to take more time on weaker enemies with the risk of them getting a lucky hit but saving up your Rage and Willpower for later, or tearing through the mooks and hopping you have enough left for the bigger fight.<br /> <br /> 4) Combat threats that require lateral tactics. Make enemies that you don't take out with damage, but through some unique weakness you have to exploit. While a bit easy for a Garou, something like the Golem where you have to damage the inscription that gave it life or it doesn't stop. Give them something that the Get's combat abilities means she's helping by keeping it busy, while the rest of the pack is trying to hit the &quot;off switch&quot; instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:18:25-07:00","id":990629,"title":"","content":"Non-combat situations force combat-focused characters to depend on their weaknesses. One scenario would be to have a few of her kinfolk get arrested by the FBI and require her to figure out how to get them out of an FBI building without backup. If she decides to use combat, let her suffer the consequences (while silver weapons are rare, I am sure that the FBI suspects enough about the supernatural world to make sure that there are a couple of specially marked automatic shotguns loaded with silver slugs for security to use against atypical threats). Otherwise, she will have to depend on her weaknesses, rather than her strengths to get through the scenario, which will allow her to grow as a character (which would also earn her a point or two of Wisdom during the next moot).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T15:05:09-07:00","id":990656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990562-dealing-with-pc-s-going-too-op?p=990629#post990629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-combat situations force combat-focused characters to depend on their weaknesses. One scenario would be to have a few of her kinfolk get arrested by the FBI and require her to figure out how to get them out of an FBI building without backup. If she decides to use combat, let her suffer the consequences (while silver weapons are rare, I am sure that the FBI suspects enough about the supernatural world to make sure that there are a couple of specially marked automatic shotguns loaded with silver slugs for security to use against atypical threats). Otherwise, she will have to depend on her weaknesses, rather than her strengths to get through the scenario, which will allow her to grow as a character (which would also earn her a point or two of Wisdom during the next moot).</div> </div> </div> </div>Going along the non-combat route works, you can also have the Garou get affected by supernatural compulsion. This is why in V;tM Ventrue can be so nasty. Take the above example and put some type of Supernatural at the FBI or whatever group you use and they are more of a Social or Mental threat. Heck if you want to use the idea of having Kinfolk kidnaped have them get involved in a Cult and when big nasty Garou come to the rescue the Kinfolk protect they bad guy and will fight the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T15:52:10-07:00","id":990667,"title":"","content":"The big thing to be careful about with increasing the non-combat challenges, is that it can annoy the player because they made a warrior that focuses on fighting and now they don't get to do that. There's nothing wrong that having situations were non-combat options are vastly superior choices, or the only acceptable choice, but too much of it and you lose the combat focused characters.<br /> <br /> In WtA this can be even more problematic because Glory Renown without combat is a minor trickle, and it puts any Glory reliant Auspice in the weeds for advancing in Rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T16:56:34-07:00","id":990687,"title":"","content":"I do not think that anyone is advocating no combat, but challenges should be balanced between physical, social, and mental. Glory gains should also be dependent on the nature of a character. A Ragabash with Glory 0 should get more temporary Glory from defeating a fomori than an Ahroun with Glory 9.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T18:47:11-07:00","id":990742,"title":"","content":"One word: Consequences.<br /> <br /> I'm currently running a long, deep campaign about Gehenna with a player who thinks he can solve any problem with enough force and time after time he's just dug himself deeper in doing so. Distancing allies, causing collateral damage, destabilising communities and power structures, getting in to confrontations with people who aren't obviously in the wrong or even are obviously in the right... solving all their problems with escalating violence is an easy way to get turned in to a pariah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","user":"ElizabethSterling","date":". 10-20-2016, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T20:05:12-07:00","id":990769,"title":"","content":"I agree. Consequences should matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T22:34:18-07:00","id":990806,"title":"","content":"All the advice about non-combat encounters is pretty great, but lets be honest, Heavy Arms is right about a Get wanting to get their claws wet.<br /> <br /> Something tells me your combats involve Mockeries/Fomori, which exist to die to werewolves' claws and fangs. Black Spiral Dancers tend to get pureed when they face an experienced Get Ahroun too. Tearing apart mooks is all well and good, but challenging or even frightening opponents are necessary once in a while. Maybe the Wyrm's forces start to recognize that their plans are foiled by rampaging Garou, and so they unleash the big guns. This gives you as a GM to come up with some really spicy combat opportunities.<br /> <br /> If you are looking for imposing antagonists, I'd recommend spirits. The obvious ones are banes, although any of the Triat's servants can get uppity. Big spirits can have heaps of essence/power (whatever you want to call 'spirit hit points' depending on edition) and they get whatever crazy suite of charms you want them to have. They are also capable of infusing cherished mortal allies, twisting the environment, and corrupting/calcifying/mutating fetishes! Most also don't give a flying fuck about the Litany and, given enough power or the right charms, might just come crashing through the Gauntlet to cause a <i>real </i>mess.<br /> <br /> If you want to have the best of both worlds, have a powerful BSM perform the rite of the Flayed God on one of these beasts and then you can have a Dancer with charms (and I tend to give them extra health levels to represent all that delicious essence, but that's just me).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-21-2016, 01:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T23:49:27-07:00","id":990825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990562-dealing-with-pc-s-going-too-op?p=990687#post990687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that anyone is advocating no combat, but challenges should be balanced between physical, social, and mental. Glory gains should also be dependent on the nature of a character. A Ragabash with Glory 0 should get more temporary Glory from defeating a fomori than an Ahroun with Glory 9.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that you're not advocating no combat, but ultimately the solution to &quot;this character is so good at combat I'm struggling to make combat hard,&quot; is not, &quot;less combat.&quot; That just makes the problem happen less, while also risking issues with both player fun in making a combat focused PC and potentially making a character that largely relies on combat for Renown/Rank.<br /> <br /> And while I don't disagree with how Renown should work, that's not the RAW and house rules on modifying Renown gains are an entirely different issue.<br /> <br /> Galliards and Ahrouns need a regular flow of Glory to progress. Combat is pretty much the only RAW way to get it, and combat also offers decent rewards in Honor and Wisdom; esp. for non-front-line characters who are more likely to be focused on those Renown types anyway. The only non-combat ways of getting Glory are solely in the realm of inter-Garou relations or Umbral quests, and those rewards aren't exactly a lot in comparison.<br /> <br /> I've been in multiple low-combat games, and those two Auspices regularly fell behind by 1-2 Ranks because of it. It's just the nature of WtA, and it's something that needs to be at least discussed with the group due to the potential impact on fun it can have if the change in combat frequency is sudden and/or ST driven.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElizabethSterling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990562-dealing-with-pc-s-going-too-op?p=990742#post990742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One word: Consequences.<br /> <br /> I'm currently running a long, deep campaign about Gehenna with a player who thinks he can solve any problem with enough force and time after time he's just dug himself deeper in doing so. Distancing allies, causing collateral damage, destabilising communities and power structures, getting in to confrontations with people who aren't obviously in the wrong or even are obviously in the right... solving all their problems with escalating violence is an easy way to get turned in to a pariah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consequences are important, but I'm not sure this really works out well.<br /> <br /> Garou already are pariahs to most of the population of the world. Their Rage means normal humans and animals shun them. This makes them insular and reliant on other Garou and kin to make up the majority of their social groups. And since they're a pre-historic warrior cult, violence and force are generally something that Garou are taught to embrace as positive traits within their isolated society. And the Garou have plenty of simple tools to keep brutish Garou in check in regards to their own social norms.<br /> <br /> One of the key elements of WtA and it's approach to consequences is that the Garou are exceedingly good at defeating immediate threats with the direct application of force and violence, but their main opponent can't really be beaten in that fashion. Garou struggle with the futility of violence in solving problems, but this is highlighted by making them really good at solving the simple problems in front of them with violence.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T06:41:33-07:00","id":990935,"title":"","content":"Multi stage combat with spirits. Think of a WoW Boss and create your own designs with objectives. The boss will have dozens/hundreds of Essence. To kill such a boss the pack needs to do accomplish certain tasks. Be creative when designing them or let educate yourself (in other words steal if from somewhere). <br /> <br /> Another thing you can do is introducing the military by them opening a secret weapon research center close to their territory. A tank is still devastating against Garou and you create reasons for special forces to be pop up who have a high WP so the veil could be threatened big time by crinos form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T10:14:12-07:00","id":991010,"title":"","content":"Some ways to get around a garou combat monster<ul><li>Guns, Lots of Guns: Garou do their deadliest damage when in close combat, try to keep that from happening as often. A number of enemies armed with guns, keeping separated will put the garou in less of a position to chew through them quickly.</li> <li>Silver: Eventually the garou has to run into those who know their weakness, and many garou learn that the hard way when they are used to shrugging off bullets but find themselves with a gut full of silver shot.</li> <li>Authorities (Police, FBI, etc): You did not mention where these fights were taking place, so I will assume outside of most mortal eyes. Try to set the fight in the city, and the garou have to worry about the police showing up (this is where the way humans process through delirium helps, since they dont see a werewolf but rather a gang member doped up on pcp assaulting people and could call the police). If your garou starts killing cops and those consequences are going to catch up quick, especially since the strange officer deaths are going to attract the attention of those 'in the know' (Pentex, FBI supernatural investigators, Hunters, Technocracy, etc).</li> <li>Go after the Brain: If the garou soaks damage like a sponge, then go after the mind. Fomori powers like Mind Blast (which can immobilize a foe), Sanity Rending (which can inflict a mental disorder), Stasis Touch (prevents shapechanging). Vampiric powers like Dominate, and Dementation. Mages with the Mind Sphere. It doesn't matter how tough the body is if the garou in question is standing there drooling.</li> <li>Go after the Family: Eventually chewing through enemies will lead to grudges, the bearers of the grudges are going to start investigating the garou. If they can trace connections such as kinfolk or other important points of interest and will begin moving against those.</li> <li>Don't Fight: As mentioned above, while combat is important to WtA its important to stress the other aspects of garou responsibilities many of which require them to not be murder machines.</li> <li>It's A Trap!: Lure the garou to a warehouse, foundry, or other structure that can be reinforced and sealed and light the place on fire. Not only does the garou have to worry about whatever foes are locked in there with them as well as any other nasty surprises, but also the ever present and growing danger of the flames and debris.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T12:03:34-07:00","id":991056,"title":"","content":"If you have an OP Garou, just take off the gloves and start throwing in threats that force them to avoid direct combat. Fomori with Horror [7] can cause Delirium in Werewolves, meaning that Werewolves with a Willpower of 6- will turn tail and run. Brain Eating [6] is another possibility, it causes permanent attribute damage to Garou (though it may be resisted with the Willpower of the Garou), and Malleate [6] can be used to liquefy even Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T19:37:49-07:00","id":991226,"title":"","content":"Everyone said something valid for this. But, at the end, you have to start yourself: talk to the player. Talk about strategic combat, about being superlatively effective in combat, about dangerous threats, about other kinds of non-combative challenges, within and without combat proper.<br /> <br /> And them simply ask what she likes and what she wants. I saw players that would like all of those. I have one that would make a killer-machine for the sole purpose of being challenged on every other aspect and almost never in combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T16:06:48-07:00","id":991574,"title":"","content":"I generally require characters to avoid hyperspecialization. They have to find people better than them to train up their Traits or else they have to spend twice as much xp to build up the Trait. A lot of my sessions have begun with players asking &quot;Where do I find someone with X at level 5?&quot;, which makes my job as an ST much easier. The fact that a give xp for the session people spend trying to find a teacher also makes life easier for my PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:26:25-07:00","id":991615,"title":"","content":"Depending on the game and the other players you may want to start changing the focus of the game away from stabbing everything in the face to something more political or needing more finesse to get through","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T21:49:18-08:00","id":1169570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990562-dealing-with-pc-s-going-too-op#post990562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, i got a rank 3 get of fenris. she is pretty buffed up right now. I throw her enemies but she keeps going higher and stronger (dealing massive ammounts of damage and soaking A LOT). which made me think..<br /> how do you guys deal with PC's going too high caliber? how do you make threats that they can't fight against or hold them against the ropes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that it can be frustrating as a GM when there's no &quot;Challenge&quot; to be had. But at the same time, you shouldn't punish a Get of Fenris Ahroun for basically doing it's job well.<br /> I would say look at balancing the game so there is enough non combat.<br /> In combat, offer different challenges; Put the Ahroun's best position to be defending innocents from multiple attackers, or have an enemy that is immune to physical threats (needs a ritual to be defeated, or computer hacking or something) while there are minions that need to be dealt with; you can't take everything away from the warrior, but you can focus on others being primarilly useful.<br /> <br /> Just remember; if you create a physical threat that will challenge this character, it might kill others if the Ahroun decides to split from the party before that scene.<br /> <br /> I know it's been over a year, so I'm interested with how it sorted out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T15:57:45-08:00","id":1169761,"title":"","content":"One thing I've learn as a GM is that sometimes it is OK for combat to go easy. You need to give the &quot;win&quot; to PCs who are combat gods for regular encounters (as long as there is plenty of opportunities for the other auspices to shine, and the combat god allows that to happen and not hijack everything). Not every encounter needs to be difficult or challenging. Most generic fomori, to be honest, are just there to be disposable cannon fodder.<br /> <br /> The key is to determine what combats should be challenging (generally based on important plot points or special lairs), and then figure out ways to do that.<br /> <br /> 1) Put the PCs in an environment they are not used to. Monsters can fly and attack from the air. Monsters are below ground, and the PCs can't maneuver. There are lots of hazards in the tactical terrain (like toxic waste drums, harmful chemicals) that can injure them severely. Have traps that they can set off.<br /> <br /> 2) Make the NPCs smart and aware the PCs are coming. Silver providing unsoakable aggravated damage should give most PCs a strong dose of caution and tension.<br /> <br /> 3) Have the NPCs have ways to indirectly challenge them. Attack them from remote controlled flying drones, installations, or ground vehicles. Why risk real people in this day and age?<br /> <br /> 4) Create new and interesting one off monsters for them to fight. I've found the Werewolf sourcebook antagonists to be rather uninteresting so I've stolen lots of concepts from Call of Cthulhu. Just file the serial numbers off - give the creature a new name, a slightly altered description, and make it appropriate to the setting. Since these kinds of monsters have interesting powers and abilities, they can provide a unique challenge.<br /> <br /> The GM can often not understand that his perspective and the players are not the same. A GM can go, &quot;Wow, that combat went way too easy. I need to make it more difficult.&quot; But the players are thinking, &quot;Wow, that was very intense. We didn't take many injuries, but that was a fun combat where lots of things could have gone wrong if we didn't spend all that time planning/preparing for it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T13:57:46-08:00","id":1172375,"title":"","content":"I tend to be reasonable. All actions have consequences, good and bad. Kill a prostitute, ok. Kill the Political Leader, maybe problems. Kill several NKVD officers, well, Vampires will learn what a tank and artillery-fire can do to their havens with the city in total lock-down from dusk to dawn.<br /> <br /> This neonate was pretty bad ass; Celerity, Potence, etc. And he did kill a lot of peasants, until he got corned, they surround him and he lost his head to a farm-boy with an axe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T20:43:18-08:00","id":1172508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990562-dealing-with-pc-s-going-too-op?p=1172375#post1172375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to be reasonable. All actions have consequences, good and bad. Kill a prostitute...</div> </div> </div> </div>...get the local Bone Gnawers and Black Furies on your ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T20:43:05-08:00","id":1174453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/990562-dealing-with-pc-s-going-too-op#post990562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, i got a rank 3 get of fenris. she is pretty buffed up right now. I throw her enemies but she keeps going higher and stronger (dealing massive ammounts of damage and soaking A LOT). which made me think..<br /> how do you guys deal with PC's going too high caliber? how do you make threats that they can't fight against or hold them against the ropes?</div> </div> </div> </div>An easy one is ST fiat, adjust the mob on the fly if need be, another is to shift gears so that the next so many sessions are less combat oriented","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T22:41:21-08:00","id":1174781,"title":"","content":"As others have probably said already, if your player(s) find that one type of challenge is far too easy, then chances are they're going to face more difficulty with problems of a completely different nature. How many times have we heard the story of the educated strategist claiming victory over the violent brute who, by all rights, should be able to crush them in a fair fight? The people at the top didn't get there by ruthlessly slaughtering everybody who stood in their way. They played things tactically in order to outmaneuver their enemies.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not every challenge has to be physical in nature, so feel free to throw them some curve balls when things get a little too comfortable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-10-2018, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}